<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:56:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>What is holding back Cyprus's Schengen ambitions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aea27aee6e18994360c53b0f3343fce84692dbe03966c69252e4ee3e9b6f29cf</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488--5f69812ab764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission says Cyprus is ready to join the Schengen Area. Yet questions relating to the island's division and British military bases could still complicate its path to Europe's border-free travel zone.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Starlink India launch: Why Elon Musk is still waiting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d72aae000f80aa1c4284ec3afddc20a2b08e0e031edad88cb08fd48669817213</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/starlink-india-launch-why-elon-musk-is-still-waiting/a-79643043--4f745799dbba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/starlink-india-launch-why-elon-musk-is-still-waiting/a-79643043?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite securing key approvals, the Starlink satellite internet service remains in regulatory limbo, raising questions about security clearances, competition and India’s investment climate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Iran 'highly likely' to be behind RAF Fairford incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14357fb5e6eb69148e64828b222633a5d0f370cb22f9194055bef0525763a039</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941--7cd1b910595f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham told parliament there were "strong indications" of Iranian involvement. The government summoned Iran's ambassador. The scare at RAF Fairford led to the withdrawal of USAF B-1 heavy bombers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reports arrests of 2 Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with Starlink station fire last month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad5b131fc1429234b62f697ddd0a7d37e62cece14bd06ea307438c95472f9f9a</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:56:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-las/a-79646138--0f2bfafb19a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-last-month/a-79646138?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish authorities have reported the arrests of two Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with alleged sabotage of a Starlink station last month. Prime Minister Donald Tusk called the fire an act of "hybrid warfare."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Viral videos falsely linked to Riyadh airport attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c5fb349e22edc7ec280ff9696b37fc461034b5fea092d195252e64d961dae7c</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-viral-videos-falsely-linked-to-riyadh-airport-attacks/a-79643037--a62cb3e36a4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-viral-videos-falsely-linked-to-riyadh-airport-attacks/a-79643037?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many videos claiming to show an attack on Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport have gone viral online. DW Fact check analyzes some of the most-shared footage and finds evidence it was created using AI.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can South Korea and Ukraine resolve their diplomatic spat over North Korean POWs?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48580e34833a1dc2bdf1382bf4094adf299e7d1db5c6912577e887977e048ae3</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T13:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-south-korea-and-ukraine-resolve-their-diplomatic-spat-over-north-korean-pows/a-79641352--b03ac996f9c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-south-korea-and-ukraine-resolve-their-diplomatic-spat-over-north-korean-pows/a-79641352?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul and Kyiv are trading accusations after the transfer of two North Korean POWs to South Korea. The South insists the move was to be kept secret as it seeks to avoid antagonizing Pyongyang.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hurricane Simon batters Mexico's Pacific Coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cc264ef9c24a99947316501d22b1eee1951c6c163a78c232e8aa167405a4b5c</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T06:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hurricane-simon-batters-mexico-s-pacific-coast/a-79636873--7bc21f186996.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hurricane-simon-batters-mexico-s-pacific-coast/a-79636873?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hurricane Simon is currently running parallel to Mexico's Pacific Coast, bringing heavy rainfall and strong winds to vulnerable towns.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Two high-ranking Iranian defectors give DW a rare look into the mindset of the regime's loyal servants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1894ff4985bb306a9cade3b7a7c44a94ee6c4b8d43586a4c6b625eecf10b96a6</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T05:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-high-ranking-iranian-defectors-give-dw-a-rare-look-into-the-mindset-of-the-regime-s-loyal-servan/a-79609734--2952d3ca9d0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-high-ranking-iranian-defectors-give-dw-a-rare-look-into-the-mindset-of-the-regime-s-loyal-servants/a-79609734?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Months of correspondence with two high-ranking defectors have given DW's investigative unit a rare look at the mindset of the regime's loyal servants — and revealed a clandestine circle that allegedly plots murders.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Air strikes kill dozens of gold miners on Sudan-Egypt border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f1af6b0052b17accdad2a0a64a2c65f6441e835e7df4afdd3d27b8e2895514d</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T19:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/air-strikes-kill-dozens-of-gold-miners-on-sudan-egypt-border/a-79634889--6da6858a62db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/air-strikes-kill-dozens-of-gold-miners-on-sudan-egypt-border/a-79634889?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Sudan-based rights group said 72 people were killed in a remote, disputed area known for illegal gold mining.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the Ukrainian 'volunteers' under Russian command?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d79e505fc240e5789b9e7f96b623a3b84e153ce2624656aebe34919c98345a8</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-ukrainian-volunteers-under-russian-command/a-79629555--58ee9f17fd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-ukrainian-volunteers-under-russian-command/a-79629555?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia has announced a battalion consisting of Ukrainian "volunteers." But veterans and former prisoners of war share very different accounts.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump claims Russia and Ukraine agreed to 'energy ceasefire'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2dcdfff690a9aa2247ee70c7a6e9492dafda729ff9b9aa84411d79e684a0079</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T14:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-claims-russia-and-ukraine-agreed-to-energy-ceasefire/a-79634509--966648814544.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-claims-russia-and-ukraine-agreed-to-energy-ceasefire/a-79634509?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump says both sides have agreed to stop targeting oil refineries, power plants and other energy infrastructure immediately.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Surrogacy in Georgia is booming but at what cost?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25230025a4f9392e3103507d2ee1619ab7e2d7f78c66b92f0d7a48d6773661fa</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/surrogacy-in-georgia-is-booming-but-at-what-cost/a-79629971--321e2c4c57d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/surrogacy-in-georgia-is-booming-but-at-what-cost/a-79629971?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Georgia became a hub for surrogate pregnancies after Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022. DW spoke with parents, and those who wanted to become parents, about the hidden costs of a booming industry.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Money, networks and bias: Why women struggle to win seats in US politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a673485131aa22308e9e8a4dc2b9018c53a540ffd6652bfc0a9dd81a4426d948</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/money-networks-and-bias-why-women-struggle-to-win-seats-in-us-politics/a-79625179--d768d0a80615.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/money-networks-and-bias-why-women-struggle-to-win-seats-in-us-politics/a-79625179?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is holding Congress and state governor elections. At all levels of US politics, women are underrepresented — but they may win some historic victories in the midterms on November 3.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
